    "side": [
      {
        "t": "lead",
        "text": "Most side effects are in the gut: oily spotting, gas with discharge, urgency, oily stools and sometimes loss of bowel control. Rare serious effects include severe liver injury and kidney damage from oxalate."
      },
      {
        "t": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "lead": "Gut:",
            "text": "in year 1 of trials, oily spotting 26.6% vs 1.3% on placebo, gas with discharge 23.9%, urgent need to pass stool 22.1%, fatty or oily stool 20.0%, oily evacuation 11.9%, more frequent bowel movements 10.8%, and loss of bowel control 7.7%. These usually began in the first 3 months; about half of episodes lasted under a week.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6240792b-9224-2d10-e053-2a91aa0a2c3e",
                "label": "Xenical label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jan 2026"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "lead": "Liver:",
            "text": "rare reports of severe liver injury, including liver failure, some leading to transplant or death.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6240792b-9224-2d10-e053-2a91aa0a2c3e",
                "label": "Xenical label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jan 2026"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=a2d3bd73-f3af-4ea5-a57c-66b0004cfe4f",
                "label": "Alli Drug Facts label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Mar 2026"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "lead": "Kidneys:",
            "text": "orlistat can raise oxalate in the urine and cause kidney stones or kidney damage.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6240792b-9224-2d10-e053-2a91aa0a2c3e",
                "label": "Xenical label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jan 2026"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=a2d3bd73-f3af-4ea5-a57c-66b0004cfe4f",
                "label": "Alli Drug Facts label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Mar 2026"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "lead": "Gallstones:",
            "text": "in the 4-year diabetes trial, gallstones were reported in 2.9% on orlistat and 1.8% on placebo.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6240792b-9224-2d10-e053-2a91aa0a2c3e",
                "label": "Xenical label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jan 2026"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "lead": "Vitamins:",
            "text": "it lowers absorption of some vitamins; the labels advise a multivitamin, taken at a different time from orlistat.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6240792b-9224-2d10-e053-2a91aa0a2c3e",
                "label": "Xenical label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jan 2026"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=a2d3bd73-f3af-4ea5-a57c-66b0004cfe4f",
                "label": "Alli Drug Facts label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Mar 2026"
              }
            ]
          },
